  "visualBrief": "Native reconstructed castle with three actual courtyard voids,100.27m Hausmann tower/39m platform, red-blue clocks below the platform, one main arched-window tier and small upper round lights in the dark octagonal drum, substantial rounded lead roof/open lantern/upper bulb/tall needle. Two dark west corner lantern towers, two green-copper south turrets and four pointed court stair towers. Ochre exterior/rusticated ground storey and original abstract black-white Great Court sgraffito, stepped/curved gables, red tiled roofs, small roof dormers and chimneys, three-tier Altan loggia and two-storey Small Court arcades under a raised double-curved transparent ETFE diamond net. Connected Georgenbau through-gateway and100m skewed Langer Gang/22 real open arches, upper gallery windows and abstract gold frieze. Four actual through-entry routes, closed wooden south entrance, court basin and two tournament columns. Own paving follows independent unchanged GeoSN DGM. Cathedral/covered church bridge, Zwinger, Johanneum, Taschenbergpalais, gardens, temporary works and interiors excluded.",
